course: dictionary
lesson: 114
title: Adobe: mud bricks and a company
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Adobe is mud mixed with straw and dried in the sun to make bricks. A building made of these sun-dried bricks is also called adobe. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: «In the dry Southwest the Ancestral Puebloans built houses of stone and adobe in cliffs and canyons.» The clues are houses, built, and dry. Adobe must be a building material that works well in hot, dry places.
explain: Adobe with a capital A is a different thing. It is the name of a software company that makes programs such as Photoshop and the PDF reader. A capital letter at the start of a word often means it is a name, so check the other clues too.
fact: Adobe means mud mixed with straw and dried in the sun to make bricks.
fact: Adobe can also mean a building made of these sun-dried bricks.
fact: Adobe houses are common in dry places like the south-western USA and Mexico.
fact: Adobe keeps houses cool by day and warm at night.
fact: Adobe with a capital A is the name of a software company that makes Photoshop and the PDF reader.
exercise: «In the dry Southwest the Ancestral Puebloans built houses of stone and adobe.» What is adobe in this sentence? | Metal used for roofs | Wood from tall trees | A kind of desert plant | *Mud mixed with straw and dried in the sun to make bricks
exercise: Which clue tells you «Adobe» in a sentence is a company name? | *The capital A, with programs such as Photoshop nearby | The word dry | The word bricks
exercise: Where are adobe houses most likely to be built? | A rainy island with no sunshine | A snowy mountain village | *A dry desert town in Mexico
test: «Adobe walls kept the rooms cool by day and warm at night.» Why would people build walls from adobe in a hot, dry place? | *Adobe keeps houses cool by day and warm at night | Adobe melts in the sun, so the walls stay soft | Adobe is made of metal, so it never gets hot | Adobe is only used for computer programs
test: Mia says «Adobe» is a building in every town. What is wrong with her idea? | *Adobe is only the name of a software company, so Mia is right that it is a building | Adobe is a type of tree that grows in deserts | There is nothing wrong with her idea | Adobe is not a building, it is a material for bricks, and the company is a name
exam: «Pueblo peoples still live in the Southwest today, in homes of stone and adobe.» What does adobe mean here, and which two clues helped you decide? | Adobe means a kind of rock found in cliffs | *Adobe means sun-dried mud bricks, and the clues are homes, stone and the dry Southwest | Adobe means a software company, and the clue is the word today | Adobe is a bird that lives in the desert
